<task id="011" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>ACS thread + membership ops (create thread w/ 30-day retention; Add/RemoveParticipants)</title>
    <phase>W1 — ACS Integration (server-side only)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>7</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>010</dependencies>
    <blocks>020, 041, 051</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, acs</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Net-new BFF service under `Services/Communication/Acs/` that mutates external ACS thread + membership state (create/add/remove participants) under rate limits, sets retention policy, and is a hard prerequisite for the channel provider (020), membership reconcile (041), and outbound send (051). Tag `bff-api`; external-transport mutation surface; publish-size + CVE governance applies.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-15</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build the **ACS thread + membership operations** for the messaging channel, server-side only, extending the NEW `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Acs/` folder created in task 010. Responsibilities:

    • **Thread create** — `ChatClient.CreateChatThread(...)` with a **30-day auto-delete retention** policy set at create time (FR-15; design §8.7 — keep ACS from becoming a shadow record store). Return the ACS `ChatThreadId` for the thread↔channel child-table row (task 004 schema; written by the caller in W2/W4).
    • **Membership ops** — server-side `ChatThreadClient.AddParticipants` / `RemoveParticipant`, taking the `communicationUserId` identities minted by task 010's `IAcsIdentityService`.
    • **Rate-limit + eventual-consistency discipline** — respect ACS thread limits (**10 participant-mutations / 10s** and **30 / min per thread**; 3000/min per resource); shape the API so a bulk membership reconcile (task 041) can batch without breaching them. Threads >20 participants lose read-receipts/typing — fine for R1, note for R2.

    This layer talks to ACS **only from the BFF** (NFR-04). It is a thin adapter over the ACS Chat SDK behind a Spaarke-owned interface — no ACS types leak outside `Services/Communication/`. Do NOT build the Event Grid capture path (030/031), the channel sender/archiver (020), or the Dataverse-derived membership *derivation* logic (041 owns "who should be a member"); this task owns only the ACS-side thread + participant *mechanics*. Blueprint: `Azure-Samples/communication-services-... dotnet-quickstarts` (thread/participant/send server code).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF architect for the Communication subsystem, specializing in ACS server integration. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Acs/`. Fluent in ADR-045 (Communication channel seams), ADR-028 (central credential; server-side only), ADR-010 (DI via `CommunicationModule`), ADR-032 (Null-Object kill-switch), §10 BFF Hygiene, §11 Component Justification, and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A server-side ACS thread service exists in `Services/Communication/Acs/` that (1) creates an ACS chat thread with 30-day auto-delete retention and returns its `ChatThreadId`, and (2) adds/removes participants by `communicationUserId`, respecting ACS per-thread rate limits and exposing a batch-friendly shape for the reconcile job (041). It uses task 010's `IAcsIdentityService` for identities and the injected central `TokenCredential` (ADR-028). No ACS admin capability reaches a client (NFR-04). Registered via `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010, unconditional). Build clean; unit tests pass; publish-size delta + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      With identities in place (010), the messaging channel needs the ACS-side thread container and its membership. ACS's model: the BFF (trusted service) creates the `ChatThread` and mutates participants; membership is the transport/live-delivery projection of Dataverse-derived access (task 041 computes the authorized set; this task applies it to ACS). Retention is minimized to 30 days at create time so ACS never becomes a second system of record — Dataverse `sprk_communication` is the record (design §3 principle 2, §8.7).

      This adds `Azure.Communication.Chat` (1.4.0) to the BFF — thin over `Azure.Core` (design §8.9). Rate limits are real and must shape the interface: 10 participant-mutations/10s and 30/min per thread; a naive per-participant loop in the 041 reconcile would breach them, so expose an `AddParticipants(IEnumerable&lt;...&gt;)` batch and let the caller throttle. Eventual consistency between Dataverse and ACS is expected and reconciled by 041 (event + sweep); this task just provides idempotent, rate-aware mutations.

      **§11 Component Justification (concrete cost-of-doing-nothing):** without these NEW `Acs/` thread ops there is **no chat transport container** — a message has nowhere to be sent (020/051 blocked) and membership cannot be projected onto ACS (041 blocked). The failure mode is a named contract failure (FR-15 unmet; 020/041/051 blocked), not "future flexibility." No overlap with any existing service — `Azure.Communication.Chat` is net-new (design §2). It cannot fold into the email path: email has no thread-container transport; ACS thread mechanics are channel-specific and belong behind the Communication boundary.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Acs/IAcsIdentityService.cs (from task 010 — source of `communicationUserId` identities)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/CommunicationChannelDispatcher.cs (ADR-045 seam surface — the sender in 020 calls these thread ops)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/EmailChannelSender.cs (thin-adapter-over-transport shape to mirror)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/ (add AcsThreadCreateResult / AcsMembershipChange models here)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs (register the ACS thread service, unconditional per ADR-032)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.cs (central credential precedent — inject, do NOT `new`)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-15">Create ACS threads with 30-day auto-delete retention set at create time; created threads carry the retention setting.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design §8.4">Membership ops are server-side `ChatThreadClient.AddParticipants`/`RemoveParticipant`. Respect ACS rate limits: 10 mutations/10s + 30/min per thread (3000/min per resource). Expose a batch-friendly shape so the 041 reconcile can throttle.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">Server-side only; no ACS SDK on any client; no ACS admin capability reaches a client.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">Inject the central ACS `TokenCredential` (ADR-028). MUST NOT `new` a credential / connection-string credential inline.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Thread ops sit behind the Communication service boundary and serve the channel provider (020); do not leak ACS types outside `Services/Communication/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register the ACS thread service via `CommunicationModule` only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">Registration is unconditional (Null-Object if feature-gated).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT build the Event Grid capture path (030/031), the sender/archiver (020), or the Dataverse-side membership derivation (041 owns the authorized-set computation). This task owns ACS-side thread + participant mechanics only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Membership ops take `communicationUserId` from task 010's `IAcsIdentityService`; mutations are idempotent (adding an existing participant / removing an absent one is a safe no-op).</constraint>
    <constraint source="§11">State the concrete FR-15 failure mode prevented by the new thread ops (no transport container → 020/041/051 blocked) in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§10">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta (baseline ~45.30 MB post-R4); no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/spec.md</file>
