    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Thin adapter over an external transport" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/EmailChannelSender.cs">
        Wrap the ACS Chat SDK behind a Spaarke-owned interface + result models; keep ACS types inside `Services/Communication/`.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Central credential injection (ADR-028)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Auth/ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.cs">
        Resolve the ACS `TokenCredential` from DI and pass it to the ACS `ChatClient` constructor; never `new` a credential.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Unconditional Communication DI (ADR-010/032)" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs">
        Register the ACS thread service here, unconditional (Null-Object if gated).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read design §8.1/§8.4/§8.7 (trusted-service model, membership rate limits, retention) + spec FR-15/NFR-04/NFR-05, and `.claude/agent-memory/researcher/acs-chat-integration-2026-07-16.md` if present. Read task 010's `IAcsIdentityService` to consume the identity source.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `CommunicationChannelDispatcher.cs` + `EmailChannelSender.cs` (seam/adapter shape) and `ManagedIdentityCredentialFactory.cs` (central-credential pattern). Confirm task 004's thread↔channel child table expects an ACS `ChatThreadId` string.</step>
    <step order="3">Add `Azure.Communication.Chat` (1.4.0) to `Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj`; verify it restores over the existing `Azure.Core` + the `Azure.Communication.Identity` added in 010.</step>
    <step order="4">Define the thread abstraction in `Services/Communication/Acs/`: `IAcsThreadService` — `CreateThreadAsync(topic, initialParticipants, retention=30d)` → `AcsThreadCreateResult { ChatThreadId }`; `AddParticipantsAsync(chatThreadId, IEnumerable&lt;communicationUserId&gt;)`; `RemoveParticipantAsync(chatThreadId, communicationUserId)`. Batch-friendly Add signature for the 041 reconcile. Add result/model types under `Services/Communication/Models/`.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement `AcsThreadService` wrapping `ChatClient`/`ChatThreadClient` — constructed from the DI-injected central `TokenCredential` + ACS endpoint (ADR-028, NFR-05). `CreateThreadAsync` sets the **30-day auto-delete retention** at create time (FR-15). Membership ops are idempotent (add-existing / remove-absent are safe no-ops); surface ACS rate-limit responses (429) as retryable so the caller can throttle within the 10/10s + 30/min per-thread budget.</step>
    <step order="6">Ensure identities are resolved via task 010's `IAcsIdentityService` (create-if-missing) before add — never pass a raw Entra id to ACS. Keep the batch shape so 041 can chunk to stay under the rate limit.</step>
    <step order="7">Register `IAcsThreadService` in `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010), unconditional (ADR-032 Null-Object if gated). Confirm no ACS type escapes `Services/Communication/` (grep the API layer).</step>
    <step order="8">Write unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`: (a) `CreateThreadAsync` sets 30-day retention (assert the create options); (b) Add/Remove are idempotent; (c) a batch Add of &gt;10 participants is chunked/throttle-aware (assert the batching shape, not a live ACS call); (d) the service is constructed from the injected credential (no `new` credential); (e) no ACS admin capability is exposed on any client DTO (NFR-04).</step>
    <step order="9">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Acs`; build clean, tests green.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/msg-011-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline (NFR-01). `Azure.Communication.Chat` is thin over `Azure.Core` — expect a small delta; justify if ≥+5 MB.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE from the ACS Chat package add.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus: retention set at create, rate-limit-aware batch shape, idempotent mutations, credential injected not `new`'d, ACS types don't leak); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (ADR-028, ADR-045, ADR-010/032, NFR-04/05, §11). Resolve Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path — shared `Services/Communication/`; coordinate with email-r4 + notification-spine-r1).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (011 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (retention mechanism used, batch/throttle shape, idempotency handling, publish-size delta).</step>
  </steps>

