  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`IAcsThreadService` + `AcsThreadService` exist in `Services/Communication/Acs/`; the only new ACS SDK added is `Azure.Communication.Chat`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`CreateThreadAsync` creates a thread with 30-day auto-delete retention set at create time and returns the ACS `ChatThreadId` (FR-15); a test asserts the retention option.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`AddParticipantsAsync`/`RemoveParticipantAsync` mutate membership by `communicationUserId` (resolved via task 010's identity service), are idempotent, and expose a batch-friendly shape sized for the ACS 10/10s + 30/min per-thread limit.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The ACS client is constructed from the DI-injected central `TokenCredential`; no `new` credential appears inline (ADR-028 / NFR-05).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No ACS admin capability / thread-mutation surface is exposed to any client (NFR-04 — grep/diff-verifiable); no client-side ACS SDK is added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Service registered via `CommunicationModule`, unconditional (ADR-010/032); ACS types do not leak outside `Services/Communication/`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; tests green; publish-size delta reported vs ~45.30 MB (small); no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 010 (identities — thread ops take `communicationUserId`). Blocks 020 (messaging sender creates/uses the thread), 041 (reconcile applies the Dataverse-derived authorized set via these Add/Remove ops), and 051 (outbound send targets a thread).

    Strict scope: ACS-side thread + participant *mechanics* only. This task does NOT decide *who* should be a member (041 derives the authorized set from Dataverse via ADR-034), does NOT capture inbound events (030/031), and does NOT persist any `sprk_communication` row (020/051). If a step seems to require `MembershipResolverService` or an Event Grid handler, stop — that is 041 / 030.

    Rate limits are load-bearing: design the batch Add so the 041 reconcile can chunk under 10/10s + 30/min per thread. Threads >20 participants lose read-receipts/typing — acceptable for R1 matter threads; note for R2 in `current-task.md`.

    Reference impl to copy: the ACS dotnet quickstarts (thread/participant/send server code).
  </notes>

